=== QR001 | reverse asc is desc
r:{[p] reverse asc p}

=== QR001 | and reverse desc is asc
r:{[p] reverse desc p}

=== clean | first asc is not min: asc puts a null first and min skips it
r:{[p] first asc p}

=== QR002 | an identity lambda under each
r:{[p] {x} each p}

=== QR002 | spelled with the each adverb too
r:{[p] {x}'[p]}

=== clean | each-prior is something else
r:{[p] {x}':[p]}

=== QR003 | distinct after sorting distinct items
r:{[p] distinct asc distinct p}

=== QR004 | one arithmetic operation with a number, which is atomic
r:{[p] {x+1} each p}

=== QR004 | the number on the left
r:{[p] {2*x} each p}

=== clean | a lambda that is not one atomic operation needs its each
r1:{[p] {x,1} each p}
r2:{[p] {x+y} each p}
r3:{[p] {sum x} each p}

=== clean | sum is not +/: it skips nulls
r:{[p] {x+y}/[p]}
